{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794478931,"nonce":"sV+w3+0Ga2ite+iBajUPwblDu70=","message":"Text landed locally in 2589c64fde4e2fca39d375ec9a6165828203489e (not pushed).\n\nEach bound node now has two rows: 2n for its batch primitives (group opacity stays a layer command) and 2n+1 for the glyphs under it, which draw outside any layer and take the fade as an alpha ratio; a row's parent is the same kind of row of the nearest bound ancestor, found from the layout tree, so a node that moves only text has a slot too. The cached motion glyph batch records which node owns each run. At a full paint the dynamic batch and the glyphs are given their slots together, the only moment both are baked at the same pose; later frames write rows only, and decline (releasing the slots) if any cached glyph lacks one, which is what a recollect at the current pose leaves.\n\nResult: the label of a card moves with it on rows alone. Labelled translate, scale, turn and nested scenes, and every scene without text, match the vector paint (nested from its second frame; see the new issue 1c8110a for the first). This also fixes e238df7 for the table path: the cached label no longer stays where the last full paint put it.\n\nStill declined: an opacity group with text in it (labelled fade and all-four scenes). The node's primitives are not in the dynamic batch there, because text in a group takes the cross-stream path, so every frame is a full paint as before. SVG in a bound subtree, glyphs under a clip, and a node that has a clip of its own also decline.\n\nMistake worth knowing: I staged crates/blinc_app wholesale and the device diagnostics in ios.rs went into the commit; caught before anything left the machine, reset and recommitted without it.","files":null}]}